 "intro_html": "Use <b>raw jumbo or king prawns</b>, about <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"30\" data-b=\"40\" data-s=\"0\">30–40 g</span> each before peeling. Straighten gently so the thickest part cooks evenly. This is a thin tempura coating, without breadcrumbs. For mushrooms, see <a href=\"oyster-mushroom-tempura.html\">oyster mushroom tempura</a>.",
 "mise": [],
 "more_label": "More japanese:",
 "next": {
  "slug": "oyster-mushroom-tempura",
  "title": "Oyster mushroom tempura"
 },
 "notes": [
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>If the peeled body is over about <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"len\" data-u=\"cm\" data-a=\"2\" data-s=\"0\">2 cm</span> thick, split it lengthwise before coating, or use smaller prawns.</li><li>The displayed time is a guide; check the thickest piece instead of relying on the clock.</li></ul>",
   "title_html": "For truly huge prawns"
  },
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Do not whisk the batter smooth, coat the whole batch in advance or crowd the oil.</li><li>Keep ice outside the batter bowl, not loose in the frying pot.</li></ul>",
   "title_html": "Keep the coating light"
  },
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Try sweet potato or lotus root in <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"len\" data-u=\"mm\" data-a=\"5\" data-b=\"10\" data-s=\"0\">5–10 mm</span> slices; kabocha in thin wedges; aubergine in thin fans; asparagus spears; shiitake caps; small maitake clusters; or fresh shiso leaves, battered on one side.</li><li>Dry everything first.</li><li>Roots need longer than leaves: fry separately and test the centre for tenderness.</li></ul>",
   "title_html": "Other good tempura choices"
  }
 ],
